{
  "_comment": [
    "What people actually type when they want a category, keyed by category slug.",
    "",
    "This is the piece that makes an imported directory record findable. A scraped shop has",
    "a name, a category and a location and nothing else -- no menu, no product list. Nobody",
    "searching 'biryani' will ever match 'Paradise Restaurant' on its own text. The category",
    "knows that a restaurant is where biryani comes from, and these terms carry that onto",
    "every business and listing in it.",
    "",
    "Per category rather than per record, so a few hundred terms cover four million",
    "businesses. All three languages in one list: someone typing బిర్యానీ and someone typing",
    "biryani want the same shop.",
    "",
    "Deliberately not exhaustive. This is a starting vocabulary meant to be corrected by",
    "somebody who knows what people in Hyderabad and Warangal actually type -- and by the",
    "zero-result searches the platform will start recording."
  ],
